#
# Conformance case: cognition/calibration-forecast-series
# AC (ME12, design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md §Calibration assessment names an explicit series):
# a calibration assessment names an explicit forecast/outcome series with a scoring
# rule and reference class, kept APART from a single confidence value.
#
# Rule ex:isSeriesCalibration fires ONLY when a CognitiveAssessment has BOTH
# logic:assessmentEvidence (the series) AND logic:assessmentMethod (the scoring rule)
# in addition to being dimensioned on logic:dimensionCalibration.
#
# A bare logic:confidence value on loneConfidence carries none of those series
# attributes, so loneConfidence does NOT satisfy the rule body — proving that the
# series-based framing is distinct from a single numeric confidence expression.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/cognition/calibration-forecast-series/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

ex:ruleIsSeriesCalibration a logic:Rule ;
    logic:provenance ex:ruleIsSeriesCalibration ;
    logic:head [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate ex:isSeriesCalibration ; rdf:object "?a" ] ;
    logic:body [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate logic:assessmentDimension ; rdf:object logic:dimensionCalibration ] ,
               [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate logic:assessmentEvidence ; rdf:object "?series" ] ,
               [ rdf:subject "?a" ; rdf:predicate logic:assessmentMethod ; rdf:object "?rule" ] .
